<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khalid bin Mohammed Al Qasimi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khalid bin Mohammed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> was ruler of Sharjah from 1965, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> deposed his cousin Saqr bin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>, until 1972. He accepted a memorandum of understanding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-musa">Abu Musa</a> in November 1971 and took Sharjah into the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a> at its founding that December. He was killed in January 1972 during a coup attempt led by Saqr.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khalid-bin-mohammed-al-qasimi.jpg" alt="Khalid bin Mohammed Al Qasimi" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noor Ali Photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Group-photo-TSC-meeting-1969.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
